style.css
body {
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  background: #f4f1ea;
  color: #222;
  max-width: 800px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 24px;
}

.hero {
  background: white;
  border-radius: 16px;
  padding: 32px;
  text-align: center;
}

.hero img {
  border-radius: 50%;
}

.button {
  display: inline-block;
  background: #ff9b32;
  color: white;
  padding: 12px 24px;
  border-radius: 999px;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.button:hover {
  background: #e07800;
}

.cards {
  display: flex;
  gap: 16px;
}

.card {
  flex: 1;
  background: white;
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 20px;
}

@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .cards {
    flex-direction: column;
  }
}

The work loop: edit, save (Ctrl+S / Cmd+S), refresh the browser (F5 / Cmd+R).

Common mistakes:
All styles ignored  -  the link's href doesn't match the CSS file name (styles.css vs style.css)
Half the styles gone  -  a missing closing curly bracket breaks the rule after it
Code shows as plain text  -  the file was saved as index.html.txt
Broken picture icon  -  the img src doesn't match the image file name
Developer tools: F12 or Ctrl+Shift+I (Windows/Linux), Cmd+Option+I (Mac), or right-click, Inspect.

